{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_bena2hujq3fvke2wgcutlt5paljto7g7qcsssqiq6mxxmrnjwu6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete. Summary of what I implemented in `src/fs.rs`:\n\n- **fs_error**: Prints to stderr matching the C `perror` style, including the last OS error.\n- **fs_open**: Parses `r`/`w` flags from the C-style mode string, returning `Option<OwnedFd>` (None on failure). `w` mode truncates/creates.\n- **fs_close**: Drops the `OwnedFd`, which closes the underlying fd.\n- **fs_rename / fs_stat / fs_fstat / fs_lstat**: Thin wrappers over `std::fs` equivalents.\n- **fs_ftruncate / fs_truncate**: Use `File::set_len`.\n- **fs_chown / fs_fchown / fs_lchown**: Use `std::os::unix::fs::{chown, fchown, lchown}` on Unix; return `Unsupported` on non-Unix.\n- **fs_size**: Returns metadata length.\n- **fs_fsize**: Mirrors the C behavior of saving and restoring the cursor position via `seek`.\n- **fs_read / fs_nread / fs_fread / fs_fnread**: Read full file or up to `n` bytes; truncate buffer to actual bytes read.\n- **fs_write / fs_nwrite / fs_fwrite / fs_fnwrite**: Truncate-write to a path or write into a borrowed fd; clamp `len` to the actual data slice length.\n- **fs_mkdir**: Uses `DirBuilder` with the given mode on Unix.\n- **fs_rmdir**: Wraps `fs::remove_dir`.\n- **fs_exists**: Returns a `bool` via `Path::exists`.\n\nA private helper `file_from_borrowed_fd` clones the borrowed `OwnedFd` (via `try_clone`/`dup`) so the `File` instance used internally can be dropped without closing the caller's fd. No `unsafe`, no FFI, no placeholders. Both debug and release builds compile cleanly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":182,"cache_read_input_tokens":28588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":182,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_managem